   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "An improper integral is used to decide whether the series \\( \\sum_{n=3}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{n(\\ln n)^{2}} \\) converges. Take f(x) to be the series' general term with n replaced by x, and the lower limit of integration to be the series' starting index. Find the exact value of the improper integral of f from that lower limit to infinity."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Divide",
         1,
         [
            "Ln",
            3
         ]
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Take \\( f(x) = \\frac{1}{x(\\ln x)^{2}} \\), so \\( f(n) \\) is the general term. On \\( [3, \\infty) \\), \\( f \\) is positive, continuous, and decreasing, so the integral test applies.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            1,
            [
               "Multiply",
               "x",
               [
                  "Power",
                  [
                     "Ln",
                     "x"
                  ],
                  2
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The series starts at \\( n = 3 \\), so the matching integral is \\( \\int_{3}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{x(\\ln x)^{2}} \\, dx = \\lim_{b \\to \\infty} \\int_{3}^{b} \\frac{1}{x(\\ln x)^{2}} \\, dx \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "An antiderivative is \\( F(x) = - \\frac{1}{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}} \\), so \\( \\int_{3}^{b} \\frac{1}{x(\\ln x)^{2}} \\, dx = \\frac{1}{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}} - \\frac{1}{\\ln{\\left(b \\right)}} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Divide",
               1,
               [
                  "Ln",
                  3
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Negate",
               [
                  "Divide",
                  1,
                  [
                     "Ln",
                     "b"
                  ]
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "As \\( b \\to \\infty \\), \\( F(b) \\to 0 \\), so the integral converges to \\( \\frac{1}{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}} \\). This number is the value of the integral, not the sum of the series.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            1,
            [
               "Ln",
               3
            ]
         ]
      }
